WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:02.330
Please.

00:02.330 --> 00:04.940
May I request an audience with the duke?

00:05.560 --> 00:08.020
It is necessary for the creation 
of the sugar confection.

00:08.440 --> 00:12.040
If possible, I'd like for it to be 
just His Grace and I, alone.

00:14.450 --> 00:22.470
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

00:29.170 --> 00:31.890
<i>It's all right</i>

00:31.890 --> 00:35.730
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

00:35.730 --> 00:42.230
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

00:42.230 --> 00:48.810
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

00:48.810 --> 00:58.130
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

00:58.570 --> 01:01.790
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

01:01.790 --> 01:04.910
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

01:05.190 --> 01:12.020
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

01:12.020 --> 01:14.720
<i>That miracle</i>

01:14.970 --> 01:21.680
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

01:21.680 --> 01:27.980
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

01:27.980 --> 01:35.100
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

01:35.100 --> 01:43.330
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

01:45.080 --> 01:48.840
There is something I would like to ask 
for the sake of making the sugar confection.

01:50.850 --> 01:54.210
The lady in the portrait... 
Please tell me her name.

01:56.870 --> 01:58.720
Why do you require a name?

01:59.150 --> 02:01.180
In order to give the lady form.

02:01.690 --> 02:06.680
I believe I need to know even the things 
which are not depicted in the portrait.

02:07.470 --> 02:09.100
And then you can make it?

02:10.470 --> 02:11.560
I don't know.

02:13.300 --> 02:16.490
Your question intrudes upon my memories.

02:17.890 --> 02:20.360
If you dare to enter there, 
stirring things up...

02:20.360 --> 02:22.220
and are still unable to create it,

02:22.220 --> 02:24.260
I'll have you pay for it with your death.

02:24.700 --> 02:26.540
Are you prepared to accept that?

02:28.560 --> 02:30.500
I cannot be prepared to die.

02:31.050 --> 02:33.800
I have made a promise to a dear friend.

02:33.800 --> 02:36.210
And I have something I must say, as well.

02:36.900 --> 02:38.380
Which is why I won't die!

02:38.380 --> 02:40.060
And because I am resolved to that,

02:40.060 --> 02:42.900
I will <i>not</i> fail to create the piece!

02:45.640 --> 02:47.140
Christina.

02:47.780 --> 02:50.620
Is that the lady's name?

02:50.620 --> 02:51.560
It is.

02:52.180 --> 02:54.360
What is her proper fairy name?

02:55.040 --> 02:56.970
Lealis Cil Eril.

02:57.610 --> 03:00.570
Why don't you call her by her true name?

03:01.600 --> 03:03.500
Because she desired it to be so.

03:04.090 --> 03:06.600
She wanted to be called by a humanlike name,

03:07.080 --> 03:08.570
and asked me to give her one.

03:09.830 --> 03:13.020
That was when she'd only just been born.

03:16.000 --> 03:19.700
She gazed out idly at the wave crests 
from which she'd been born.

03:20.580 --> 03:25.320
That she would be caught 
by humans and hurt was lamentable,

03:25.320 --> 03:26.890
so I brought her back to the castle.

03:27.590 --> 03:29.900
Where is Lady Christina now?

03:31.030 --> 03:32.360
Dead and vanished.

03:33.720 --> 03:35.520
A year and a half ago.

03:36.820 --> 03:38.380
<i>He was in love with her.</i>

03:39.300 --> 03:41.720
<i>And even now,</i>

03:42.420 --> 03:46.200
<i>somewhere in his heart, 
he's still calling her name.</i>

03:47.170 --> 03:51.190
I'd heard that he'd been acting strangely, 
but I hadn't realized it was that bad.

03:51.640 --> 03:55.130
And I can't help wondering about the fact 
that Lady Christina isn't with him.

03:55.450 --> 03:56.520
A lover?

03:59.510 --> 04:00.590
A fairy lover.

04:02.020 --> 04:03.300
With blue hair?

04:03.600 --> 04:06.160
Yes. Did you see her in the castle?

04:06.160 --> 04:07.850
A portrait of her.

04:07.850 --> 04:11.770
The girl was ordered to create 
a sugar confection using it as a model.

04:12.090 --> 04:14.010
Not the lady herself?

04:15.700 --> 04:16.730
Challe.

04:16.730 --> 04:19.230
How long do fairies born of the sea live?

04:19.630 --> 04:23.360
The lives of water fairies 
are unstable, so it varies.

04:23.360 --> 04:27.240
There are some who live for hundreds of years, 
and some who vanish after only a few.

04:27.610 --> 04:28.800
What about sugar confections?

04:28.800 --> 04:31.620
Eating those extends 
a fairy's life, doesn't it?

04:32.030 --> 04:35.130
There aren't many sugar confections 
with that sort of power.

04:35.690 --> 04:38.670
With something you've made, it's possible...

04:38.670 --> 04:41.130
but it would just be a
 few weeks to a few months.

04:41.570 --> 04:42.910
I see...

04:43.660 --> 04:45.830
She's disappeared.

04:47.330 --> 04:48.930
That's why the duke is...

04:50.050 --> 04:52.960
Why would a human be bothered 
over something like that?

04:52.960 --> 04:56.860
They simply buy another companion fairy 
and satisfy themselves that way.

04:59.750 --> 05:02.120
She wasn't a companion fairy.

05:03.160 --> 05:06.150
No one can possibly take her place.

05:07.240 --> 05:12.450
She was always saying that water fairies 
never know how long they will live.

05:16.180 --> 05:18.760
<i>I didn't understand at all.</i>

05:19.260 --> 05:21.760
<i>What the duke truly desires is...</i>

05:22.800 --> 05:25.590
May I bring my tools here?

05:26.040 --> 05:28.720
I will perform my work 
in your presence, Your Grace.

05:29.280 --> 05:33.220
As I ask questions about Lady Christina, 
I will give her form!

05:35.320 --> 05:39.100
What the duke has been bearing
 alone is impossible to fathom.

05:39.840 --> 05:43.630
House Alburn did not rebel 
against House Millsland.

05:43.630 --> 05:46.530
They fought for His Majesty, Edmond II.

05:46.860 --> 05:48.520
And yet, what happened next?

05:48.520 --> 05:51.920
The royal family sucks up 
all the trade profits,

05:51.920 --> 05:55.250
and they were obliged 
to pay a monthly courtesy visit.

05:55.630 --> 05:59.580
How much must they have resented 
the treatment they'd been dealt.

06:00.080 --> 06:02.240
It was she who soothed that anger.

06:02.240 --> 06:03.750
Her alone.

06:06.480 --> 06:08.880
Someone to take on all that 
resentment and bitterness?

06:08.880 --> 06:11.740
Such a fairy must have been happy indeed.

06:11.740 --> 06:14.430
Yes, I do believe she was happy.

06:15.560 --> 06:18.730
I've made many 
sugar confections for the duke.

06:19.300 --> 06:22.440
I heard that all of them were given to her.

06:23.290 --> 06:25.450
And she said it herself.

06:25.450 --> 06:29.500
She said that, for the duke's sake, she'd 
like to live even the slightest bit longer.

06:30.790 --> 06:32.380
For the duke's sake?

06:33.320 --> 06:37.530
She was probably worried 
that things might turn out this way.

06:40.880 --> 06:41.670
What's going on?

06:43.140 --> 06:46.630
Viscount, the earl's troops 
are on the road ahead.

06:47.510 --> 06:49.090
That old man...

06:50.440 --> 06:51.640
Earl of Downing!

06:51.950 --> 06:53.850
Mercury, is it?

06:53.850 --> 06:56.880
Your attempts at persuasion 
were a waste of time, I see.

06:56.880 --> 06:58.300
You were aware?

06:59.140 --> 07:02.590
We knew of your connections 
to House Alburn even before

07:02.590 --> 07:04.480
you were made Silver Sugar Viscount.

07:05.170 --> 07:08.340
However, we will allow 
no further interference!

07:08.340 --> 07:11.070
The last sparks of rebellion 
in the kingdom must be extinguished.

07:11.390 --> 07:13.000
I will not interfere.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.660
However, Anne Halford is in the castle.

07:15.660 --> 07:17.610
Really? Her?

07:18.080 --> 07:19.370
That is unfortunate.

07:19.930 --> 07:22.940
All we can do is hope that 
she has hidden herself well.

07:22.940 --> 07:23.710
But...

07:30.000 --> 07:31.160
That girl...

07:32.230 --> 07:32.890
Hey.

07:33.390 --> 07:35.510
Is this an acquaintance of yours?

07:36.640 --> 07:38.970
Apparently, one of the cavalrymen caught it.

07:38.970 --> 07:39.850
Open it.

07:41.540 --> 07:42.240
Hup!

07:42.240 --> 07:44.400
Whoops! Ha ha!

07:44.780 --> 07:46.570
Mithril Lid Pod.

07:46.570 --> 07:50.120
He seems to have eaten 
all of the soup as he hid inside.

07:50.120 --> 07:53.710
That's not it! I mean, I did, but... 
It isn't like that!

07:53.710 --> 07:57.470
I was trying to fulfill my mission, 
but then I got hungry.

07:57.470 --> 07:58.660
What's happened to her?

07:59.220 --> 08:03.340
That's right! I came 
looking for you for her sake!

08:03.790 --> 08:04.580
For me?

08:05.120 --> 08:07.190
Because Anne is calling for you.

08:07.600 --> 08:10.550
Because she wants you to come back.

08:10.550 --> 08:13.440
Are you stupid? 
She's the one who told me to leave.

08:13.440 --> 08:16.510
Do you really think Anne would 
<i>seriously</i> tell you to leave?!

08:15.800 --> 08:16.510
You little...

08:16.840 --> 08:20.800
That was because that Jonas 
threatened Anne and made her say it!

08:20.800 --> 08:21.550
What?

08:21.550 --> 08:25.500
Jonas stole my wing 
and tore you away from Anne!

08:25.500 --> 08:28.110
And he used that to allow himself to escape!

08:28.110 --> 08:31.190
Anne has been calling for you all this time!

08:33.320 --> 08:36.960
Anne stayed in the castle and she's been 
working on the sugar confections.

08:36.960 --> 08:41.710
The duke isn't going to let Anne 
leave until she makes something he likes.

08:41.710 --> 08:44.300
And Anne's gotten all stubborn about it.

08:45.270 --> 08:46.570
That idiot.

08:46.570 --> 08:48.010
Huh? Hey!

08:48.010 --> 08:49.500
What's all this? Hey!

08:49.500 --> 08:53.000
Hey! What is all this! Let me out!

08:49.980 --> 08:51.300
I'll come back for him!

08:53.000 --> 08:54.810
Why should I care for something like this?

08:54.810 --> 08:56.800
Something like this? 
What's that supposed to mean?

08:56.800 --> 08:58.720
I am the great Mithril Lid—

08:59.890 --> 09:02.680
Artisan, what is it that you're trying to do?

09:03.100 --> 09:05.720
I will make it exactly 
the same as Lady Christina.

09:05.720 --> 09:09.850
Her height, her face, 
her expression, everything.

09:10.560 --> 09:17.030
Your Grace, when you think of Lady Christina, 
how does she appear most often?

09:18.800 --> 09:21.340
When I think of a certain person...

09:22.980 --> 09:26.670
for some reason, I remember him looking down 
at me in a seemingly bad mood.

09:29.640 --> 09:32.980
She's relaxed, leaning against a wall.

09:33.640 --> 09:35.880
And she's smiling.

09:36.520 --> 09:37.690
I see.

09:41.890 --> 09:42.940
Your Grace.

09:44.790 --> 09:45.560
What is it?

09:45.560 --> 09:49.240
More than 300 mounted 
troops have surrounded the castle.

09:49.240 --> 09:51.610
They're the Earl of Downing's men.

09:51.870 --> 09:53.070
What of it?

09:53.070 --> 09:55.310
They've come to demand 
the surrender of the castle,

09:55.310 --> 09:58.860
and to take you into custody, Your Grace.

09:58.860 --> 09:59.820
Have them wait.

10:00.610 --> 10:02.280
I want to see this.

10:03.830 --> 10:06.700
Why would the Earl of Downing 
take you, Your Grace?

10:07.360 --> 10:10.160
I haven't been to Lewiston 
for a year and a half.

10:10.160 --> 10:14.580
Saying that I lack loyalty must provide 
the perfect excuse to strike at me.

10:15.010 --> 10:17.610
But why? Doing something like that would...

10:17.610 --> 10:20.760
Quiet, artisan. You just 
work on creating that.

10:20.760 --> 10:22.520
But why—

10:23.260 --> 10:25.440
You couldn't possibly understand.

10:25.440 --> 10:27.760
To have every scrap of dignity ripped away...

10:27.760 --> 10:30.730
and to be forced to behave in a self-abasing 
manner. How that makes you feel!

10:31.140 --> 10:33.030
The only one who understood was her!

10:43.910 --> 10:48.040
<i>For the duke, Lady Christina 
was the only one who...</i>

10:48.780 --> 10:51.750
<i>But now she has vanished.</i>

10:52.820 --> 10:55.550
<i>And now this person is all alone.</i>

10:56.230 --> 10:57.690
<i>That's what he believes.</i>

11:00.520 --> 11:01.670
<i>I want to make this.</i>

11:04.150 --> 11:07.290
<i>I want to make the one thing 
the duke desires.</i>

11:09.420 --> 11:12.900
<i>And I want to depict that person's 
feelings just as they are.</i>

11:17.650 --> 11:18.860
I will have her back.

11:20.480 --> 11:21.410
Challe?

11:22.810 --> 11:23.530
What?

11:30.550 --> 11:32.340
Challe...

11:32.340 --> 11:33.420
Are you real?

11:34.740 --> 11:36.630
Your idiocy is astounding.

11:40.400 --> 11:41.340
Challe...

11:42.080 --> 11:44.890
Mithril Lid Pod told me everything.

11:45.640 --> 11:47.530
He told you?

11:48.550 --> 11:52.680
Challe, I'm so sorry. Back then, I...

11:52.680 --> 11:54.270
There is no need to apologize.

11:54.840 --> 11:57.430
More important right now is that 
we're going and leaving this castle.

11:58.160 --> 12:00.600
But the sugar confection...

12:02.750 --> 12:05.550
I will not allow this artisan to leave.

12:05.550 --> 12:09.950
She will stay here 
until she makes what I seek.

12:09.950 --> 12:12.620
Then I shall cut you down here and now.

12:12.620 --> 12:13.460
Wait, Challe!

12:13.840 --> 12:15.850
And you, too, Your Grace. Please, wait.

12:15.850 --> 12:18.570
I will continue my work, so—

12:18.570 --> 12:19.460
Are you in your right mind?!

12:19.930 --> 12:23.850
I'm serious! I want to make 
a sugar confection of this fairy.

12:24.160 --> 12:25.610
What are you trying to do?

12:25.610 --> 12:27.900
I took on this work! That's why...

12:28.880 --> 12:31.390
This castle is surrounded by soldiers!

12:31.390 --> 12:33.310
If they storm this place...

12:33.310 --> 12:34.330
I know.

12:34.330 --> 12:35.470
It's dangerous!

12:35.470 --> 12:36.770
I know that, too.

12:37.080 --> 12:40.550
But I cannot abandon my work unfinished!

12:46.180 --> 12:47.240
You are exasperating.

12:52.000 --> 12:55.290
Make it, then. But I will stay here, too.

12:58.690 --> 13:00.170
Will that be all right?

13:01.810 --> 13:02.840
Very well.

13:03.810 --> 13:04.780
Now, work.

13:16.600 --> 13:19.270
It looks very like her.

13:20.160 --> 13:22.420
But the color of her eyes is wrong.

13:23.150 --> 13:24.460
They're silver.

13:24.460 --> 13:27.490
And they have a sense of translucence, 
like light striking and reflecting off...

13:27.920 --> 13:30.730
If she had those eyes, she would...

13:33.650 --> 13:35.160
That is a sugar confection.

13:35.680 --> 13:38.060
What is the point of having 
something like that made?

13:38.540 --> 13:44.380
Fairies are born when living things gaze 
at an object and that energy condenses.

13:44.380 --> 13:46.800
If I gaze at this,

13:46.800 --> 13:48.700
will something be born?

13:49.310 --> 13:51.100
Don't you think it's possible?

13:51.100 --> 13:52.750
It can't be...

13:52.750 --> 13:56.810
You think that Lady Christina 
might be born once more from this?

13:57.260 --> 14:00.310
Have you ever witnessed 
the moment a fairy disappears?

14:01.870 --> 14:07.780
That which made up her form turned to 
motes of light and melted into thin air.

14:10.770 --> 14:16.060
Then all that needs happen is for that 
which melted into air to be given form again.

14:17.410 --> 14:18.460
Not possible.

14:19.120 --> 14:21.310
That which is lost cannot be resurrected.

14:21.310 --> 14:23.960
No matter how much you wail or wish for it.

14:24.520 --> 14:26.350
Even if you keep gazing at that thing,

14:26.350 --> 14:30.180
a strange, warped fairy will be born 
from it, and that will be the end of it!

14:30.180 --> 14:32.010
I will <i>not</i> allow you to say any more!

14:32.010 --> 14:32.890
It is the truth!

14:32.890 --> 14:34.420
Don't, Challe!

14:39.520 --> 14:41.140
So, we didn't make it in time.

14:42.190 --> 14:43.460
Your Grace...

14:46.030 --> 14:47.000
What are you doing?

14:47.000 --> 14:49.320
I might be able to make a silver color!

14:49.320 --> 14:51.510
You're still planning on working 
when all this is going on?

14:52.280 --> 14:55.200
There is no need for you to play along 
with this man's delusions!

14:55.530 --> 14:59.130
I'm not playing along! This is my work!

14:59.130 --> 15:02.890
It's the only thing I can do, 
and it's what I take pride in.

15:07.030 --> 15:08.420
You are an idiot.

15:08.940 --> 15:13.350
I think I must be. 
But... I want to see this through!

15:13.980 --> 15:15.720
If that is your wish,

15:16.710 --> 15:19.680
then work until you are completely satisfied.

15:23.320 --> 15:25.420
The Duke of Philax is in the room above!

15:25.420 --> 15:26.470
Stop.

15:28.320 --> 15:30.330
I cannot allow you to pass.

15:39.750 --> 15:40.900
Ow!

15:45.910 --> 15:48.540
The Duke of Philax's warrior fairy?

15:48.540 --> 15:49.970
Hey there! Stop what you're doing!

15:50.820 --> 15:51.930
Silver Sugar Viscount?

15:52.250 --> 15:54.970
We have permission from the Earl of Downing.

15:54.970 --> 15:58.630
Challe, I'd heard that you went off 
without warning to rescue Anne,

15:59.040 --> 16:01.230
but why are you protecting Alburn?

16:01.230 --> 16:03.700
I'm not protecting him.

16:03.700 --> 16:05.940
However, for the time being, 
I will not allow anyone to pass.

16:07.830 --> 16:09.210
Please understand.

16:09.210 --> 16:13.000
The more time passes, the more 
it appears that Alburn is resisting.

16:13.000 --> 16:13.910
It makes it worse for him.

16:14.330 --> 16:17.490
I'm sorry, but this is what she wishes.

16:23.870 --> 16:27.290
<i>Right here. Here in this silver sugar.</i>

16:30.800 --> 16:33.340
<i>I'm begging you, please appear!</i>

16:41.600 --> 16:42.750
This is...

16:58.740 --> 16:59.960
It's her.

17:06.720 --> 17:07.720
Artisan.

17:08.200 --> 17:10.010
I never asked your name.

17:10.930 --> 17:13.840
It's Halford. I'm Anne Halford.

17:14.430 --> 17:18.150
This is what I wanted, Halford.

17:19.740 --> 17:23.130
No matter how foolish 
my desire might be, I wanted this.

17:23.940 --> 17:25.340
I simply wanted it.

17:28.180 --> 17:30.150
I wanted to see her again.

17:30.880 --> 17:33.360
No one has proven it.

17:33.720 --> 17:37.790
Your Grace, if you think of 
Lady Christina and keep gazing at it,

17:37.790 --> 17:40.080
then one day, something might happen.

17:40.490 --> 17:43.540
No one has proven that it won't happen!

17:46.560 --> 17:49.540
Even if those are only words of comfort, 
they make me happy.

17:50.640 --> 17:52.250
The promised gold.

17:52.620 --> 17:55.860
Take this and return to your fairy.

17:55.860 --> 17:56.780
Go now.

18:00.030 --> 18:01.020
Halford.

18:03.560 --> 18:06.980
You are a magnificent sugar artisan.

18:09.430 --> 18:10.440
Challe!

18:12.870 --> 18:13.830
Challe!

18:29.910 --> 18:32.700
Challe. Th-Thank you.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.840
You're not hurt, are you, Anne?

18:35.840 --> 18:36.910
Hugh?

18:36.910 --> 18:38.890
Why are you here?

18:38.890 --> 18:40.970
There were certain circumstances.

18:40.970 --> 18:43.560
I've come to take 
the Duke of Philax into custody.

18:43.560 --> 18:44.600
Is he up there?

18:45.400 --> 18:48.060
Yes. He's with a sugar confection.

18:49.320 --> 18:50.360
I see.

18:51.310 --> 18:52.170
Let's go.

18:55.830 --> 18:56.700
Oh.

19:00.200 --> 19:01.530
Challe?

19:01.530 --> 19:03.440
For the moment, don't move.

19:03.440 --> 19:05.070
But... Oh!

19:06.040 --> 19:07.800
Don't make me worry so much.

19:08.230 --> 19:09.270
I'm sorry.

19:09.980 --> 19:13.110
But I'm a sugar artisan, so...

19:13.110 --> 19:13.960
Anne.

19:15.960 --> 19:19.980
That's the second time...
you've called me by my name.

19:21.350 --> 19:23.470
You remember how many times?

19:23.470 --> 19:24.970
Well, because it makes me happy.

19:28.900 --> 19:29.930
Challe.

19:31.320 --> 19:34.540
I want you to stay with me. From now on, too.

19:35.120 --> 19:36.170
Is that all right?

19:48.370 --> 19:49.910
Hello, ma'am!

19:49.910 --> 19:52.810
I heard everything! It's so amazing!

19:52.810 --> 19:53.960
Amazing?

19:53.960 --> 19:55.960
The Duke of Philax's sugar sculpture!

19:56.450 --> 20:00.000
I was shocked when I heard that 
the duke had been taken into custody.

20:00.000 --> 20:03.310
Everyone said that it wouldn't be odd 
at all for him to be harshly punished.

20:03.310 --> 20:06.200
But he's only living in seclusion under 
the Earl of Downing's supervision, right?

20:06.200 --> 20:09.390
That was quite a magnanimous way 
to deal with him, don't you think?

20:09.390 --> 20:14.330
And the rumor is that it's all because of 
the sugar confection you made him, young lady!

20:16.440 --> 20:20.730
I suppose it's true that sugar 
confections bring good fortune!

20:31.200 --> 20:32.870
Have you finished your prayers?

20:34.480 --> 20:35.380
Yes.

20:37.090 --> 20:39.740
Hoping that we can accept 
the deaths of those we love

20:40.770 --> 20:45.450
and that those of us who are left behind 
are not always trapped by sorrow.

20:46.040 --> 20:47.930
Anne!

20:47.930 --> 20:51.790
The food stand over there 
has lots of yummy-looking food!

20:51.790 --> 20:53.850
Let's go and eat, the three of us!

20:53.850 --> 20:56.270
Yay! Yahoo!

20:56.270 --> 20:57.060
Shall we go?

20:57.580 --> 20:58.360
Yes.

20:59.360 --> 21:04.900
If I Keep Gazing at You

21:16.170 --> 21:20.500
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.370 --> 21:26.640
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.640 --> 21:30.180
<i>Just as our night dreams 
are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.180 --> 21:37.250
<i>If they aren't held dear, 
they will disappear?</i>

21:37.250 --> 21:48.390
<i>No, it's because they aren't things 
that only special people can see</i>

21:48.390 --> 21:49.120
<i>That day</i>

21:49.120 --> 21:53.570
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.570 --> 21:59.130
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.130 --> 22:04.630
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.630 --> 22:08.930
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:08.930 --> 22:14.760
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.760 --> 22:26.240
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.040 --> 22:39.960
<b>The Radcliffe Workshop</b>
